# ---------- AGENTS.md ----------
build_agents_md() {
  local stack_line cmd_block
  stack_line="$(IFS=, ; echo "${STACKS[*]}")"
  cmd_block=""
  [[ -n "$BUILD_CMD" ]] && cmd_block+="- Build: \`${BUILD_CMD}\`"$'\n'
  [[ -n "$TEST_CMD"  ]] && cmd_block+="- Test:  \`${TEST_CMD}\`"$'\n'
  [[ -n "$LINT_CMD"  ]] && cmd_block+="- Lint:  \`${LINT_CMD}\`"$'\n'
  [[ -n "$DEV_CMD"   ]] && cmd_block+="- Dev:   \`${DEV_CMD}\`"$'\n'
  [[ -z "$cmd_block" ]] && cmd_block="- TODO: document build/test/lint/dev commands here."$'\n'

  cat <<EOF
# ${PROJECT_NAME}

<!-- Initialized by agent-init v${VERSION} on $(date +%Y-%m-%d) -->
<!-- Canonical project memory. Read by Codex natively; by Claude via CLAUDE.md's @AGENTS.md import. -->
<!-- Keep under ~200 lines. Both agents read this every turn. -->

## What this is

TODO: 2–3 sentences. What does it do, who uses it, what's the deploy surface?

## Stack

${stack_line}

## Build & test

${cmd_block}
## Topology

- \`src/\` — application code
- \`tests/\` — test suite
- \`.agents/\` — canonical agent config (specialists, skills, hooks, MCP)
- \`.claude/\` — generated Claude Code config (do not hand-edit)
- \`.codex/\` — generated Codex CLI config (do not hand-edit)
- TODO: document the rest

## Conventions

- Match existing patterns. Search before inventing — grep/glob first.
- New files mirror nearest-neighbor structure.
- No new dependencies without justification.
- Tests are required for new code paths.
- Edit \`.agents/\` (the source of truth), then run \`agent-init sync\` to refresh \`.claude/\` and \`.codex/\`.

## Guardrails (never do these)

- Never commit secrets, .env files, or credentials.
- Never push directly to \`main\` / \`master\`. Branch + PR.
- Never modify generated artifacts (\`dist/\`, \`build/\`, \`.next/\`, \`__pycache__/\`, \`target/\`).
- Never disable a test to get green. Fix the cause or ask.
- Never rewrite migrations that have run anywhere.

## Specialists (use them)

Defined in \`.agents/specialists/\` and rendered for both tools:

- \`planner\` — call BEFORE coding any feature touching >2 files
- \`code-reviewer\` — call AFTER a feature, before commit; catches subtle correctness/security issues
- \`test-runner\` — call instead of running tests inline; saves context
- \`debugger\` — call when a test fails or behavior is unexpected; root-cause analysis

## Skills

Cross-tool skill definitions in \`.agents/skills/\`. Both Claude and Codex read them:

- \`plan\` — decompose a request into ordered, verifiable steps
- \`review\` — review uncommitted changes for correctness/security
- \`ship\` — run tests, then commit if green (no push)

## MCP

See \`.claude/MCP_SETUP.md\` (Claude) and/or \`.codex/MCP_SETUP.md\` (Codex) for installable
servers. Logical server list lives in \`.agents/mcp.yaml\`.

## Failure modes (lessons learned)

<!-- Add as you discover them. This is the most valuable section over time. Examples: -->
<!-- - The \`users\` table has soft deletes (deleted_at); always filter unless told otherwise. -->
<!-- - Integration tests need Postgres on port 5433 (\`docker-compose up -d db\`). -->

TODO: Start populating after the first session. When an agent gets something wrong, document it here.
EOF
}

